{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T06:32:39.481Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"00cec8b639eabc53332f98bc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-26T06:32:39.481Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Issue 151 implementation: annotation uses a managed fixture; async afterEach waits for owned task settlement, child close (including pipes) and watcher close, then calls fs.promises.rm with recursive=true, force=true, maxRetries=8 and retryDelay=25. Early resource rejections are observed immediately and retained for teardown failure; permanent removal errors remain visible as aggregate failures. SDK mutation refresh runs in supported foreground test mode, and synchronous annotation subprocesses finish before teardown. Full annotation plus fixture regressions pass 28/28 on Node 24 and 28/28 on Node 22. Revert proofs: setting only cleanup maxRetries to zero makes the native ENOTEMPTY regression fail 0/1; restoring it passes 1/1. Removing only the resource join makes the child/watcher teardown regression fail 0/1 (child still running); restoring it passes 1/1. Commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"fixture cleanup retries\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"fixture teardown joins\" test/fixture-lifetime.test.ts. Existing provenance assertions are unchanged. SDK gap: PmClient has no lifecycle disposal/pending-worker drain API, so supported foreground refresh prevents detached SDK work. Exact-head full CI and Fixes #151 PR body follow after the separate session-isolation commit."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T06:32:39.481Z"}],"before_hash":"106f66de35afb05e3f93b92b9b68de32c219bd5dbeed6